✴️ Day 4 of #90DaysOfDevOps
Today i practiced important linux monitoring & service commands like ps, ps -ef, top/htop systemctl, journalctl. i also explored different
linux processes & services such as cron, networking related services.

-Process commands 

  ps - process status : display a snapshot of current process

  ps aux : show all process for all users

  ps -ef : display all format including parent process id

  top/htop : provide real time view of running process

-Service commands

 systemctl start ngnix - start the service

 systemctl status ngnix - check the service is active/inactive

-Log command

journalctl : view all logs
journalctl -f : follow logs in real time

tail -f var/log/syslog : countinousaly monitor new entries in system log
